  "notes": "The focal query follows the full assigned route (CONVERSATION_MEMBERSHIP -> CONVERSATION -> MESSAGE -> USER -> REACTION) exactly, using channels as the hub tying the membership's channel to the message's channel, and treating the fire reaction as belonging to that message's author without requiring it to be on the same message (per the design's own binding note). Because that chain by itself is channel-dependent rather than membership-row-dependent, it alone would match every #engineering membership; the auxiliary query (reusing channel_members, users, messages, channels — all within the same route's entity set) independently pins the root's user_id to the unique author of the OOM/circuit-tracer message, so only the intersection (channel=#engineering AND user=Łukasz) survives, giving the single correct membership. The actor (U01AGENBOT9) already holds memberships in #engineering, #model-research, and #core-infra, so all messages and reactions needed (the OOM message, Sophie's checkpoint message with Lukas's fire reaction, and Robert's cloud-bill message with his thumbsup reaction) are readable via documented conversations.history / reactions.get."
